        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കലാപം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കലാപം — kalāpaṁ — \"a riot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കലാപം കാരണം കടകൾ അടച്ചു. kalāpaṁ kāraṇaṁ kaṭakaḷ aṭaccu. Shops closed because of the riot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also an uproar at a meeting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of കലാപം (kalāpaṁ) in the sense of a riot is not settled. In the news it is violent disorder in a town."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
