          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആയുധം — āyudhaṁ — \"a weapon\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പോലീസ് കള്ളന്റെ കയ്യിൽ നിന്ന് ആയുധം പിടിച്ചെടുത്തു. pōlīsŭ kaḷḷanṟe kayyil ninnŭ āyudhaṁ piṭicceṭuttu. The police seized a weapon from the robber's hand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ആയുധങ്ങൾ, āyudhaṅṅaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A tool is ഉപകരണം; a weapon is ആയുധം (āyudhaṁ)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആയുധം (āyudhaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit āyudha, \"a weapon\" (CDIAL 1291), from the root yudh, \"to fight\", the root of യുദ്ധം (yuddhaṁ)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
